  "keychainMigrationAllow": "Move keys",
  "keychainMigrationBody": "WhisPaste is moving your saved keys, such as API keys, to its own, better protected place on this Mac. While it does, macOS opens a window asking for a password. Enter the password you use to log in to your Mac and click “Always Allow”. If you saved several keys, the window may appear once for each. This happens only for this one move; afterwards macOS stops asking. Your password and keys stay on your Mac, nothing is sent anywhere.",
  "keychainMigrationDeclined": "The saved keys were not moved. Until then they are missing in WhisPaste, for example API keys for transcription. Nothing was deleted. You can start the move again at any time.",
