  "onboardingPasteChipReady": "Auto-Paste ready",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxAppImage": "Auto-Paste needs a one-time permission for the virtual keyboard. Copy the command and run it once in a terminal. It writes the udev rule 71-whispaste-uinput.rules, needs administrator rights and changes the system: echo 'KERNEL==\"uinput\", SUBSYSTEM==\"misc\", TAG+=\"uaccess\"' | sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/71-whispaste-uinput.rules && sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=misc --sysname-match=uinput. The permission applies only to your signed-in session. Until then, auto-paste only copies the text.",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxClipboardFallback": "Auto-Paste is on. Until access is set up, WhisPaste puts the text on the clipboard, and you paste it yourself with Ctrl+V.",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxFlatpak": "In the Flatpak build (--device=all), the input devices of this computer are visible inside the sandbox. WhisPaste itself reads no input. If your user account may read these devices (for example as a member of the input group), the app could read other programs' keystrokes. Auto-Paste also needs a one-time command: copy it and run it once in a terminal (administrator password needed; it changes the system). If you do not want this, leave auto-paste off and paste the text by hand.",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxNative": "Auto-Paste needs your permission for the virtual keyboard. With the .deb package, choose “Allow (administrator password)” and enter your administrator password; otherwise copy the command and run it once in a terminal. You can withdraw the permission again in the settings.",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxSnap": "In the Snap build, run this once in a terminal: sudo snap connect whispaste:uinput. Until then, auto-paste only copies the text.",
  "onboardingPasteLinuxUnavailableDetail": "The text goes to the clipboard. Paste it with {shortcut}.",
  "onboardingPasteSkip": "Just copy for now, no auto-insert",
  "onboardingPasteSubtitle": "macOS will ask you in a moment whether WhisPaste may do this. Say yes, done.",
